    "translatedData": {
      "title": null,
      "subTitle": null,
      "content": "A massive whale sold off $487 million worth of BTC over 3 weeks—yet BTC is still at 65,000 pretending nothing’s wrong?\n\nCurrent price 64,974, up 0.33% in 24h. High 65,483, low 64,747. Volume 4.07B U. Looks green, but it’s still stuck hovering just below the daily sell level at 65,334.\n\nETH is even more timid—1,914, up 0.1%, volume 3.86B U. It doesn’t even bother to follow BTC’s fake moves.\n\nThe most eye-catching thing in today’s chart isn’t the gains or losses—it’s supply. That whale, over the past 3 weeks, has sold a total of 7,513 BTC, about $487 million, and just now dumped another 1,019 BTC. They’re distributing sales in batches—no big dump to crash the market. It’s basically tailor-made to crush wishful thinking.\n\nRobinhood’s on-chain assets did break $1B, with stablecoins making up 60%—money is coming in, but it’s coming in as cash management, not to catch high-risk positions at the top.\n\nBTC funding rate is +0.0059%, ETH is +0.002%—positive like they’re playing dead. Bulls don’t light the fuse; bears already have ammunition. Direction stays the same: the bearish signal still holds advantage.\n1. If BTC’s rebound can’t break above 65,334, first look for a pullback to 64,551; after losing it, the next stop is 63,800\n2. ETH’s daily sell level at 1,929 is a hard lid—1,898 can’t hold, and it will keep underperforming the broader market\n3. BNB 602 is stuck to the buy zone; liquidity is thin—don’t expect it to set the pace\n\nDon’t treat a small green candle at midday as a turnaround. The whale is still unloading; above the pivot point is the supply/sell-pressure zone. If bulls truly want a reversal, at least they need to stand firm with volume above 65,334; otherwise this rebound is just setting up position for the next cut.\n\n$BTC  daily sell level: $65334 daily buy point: $64551\n$ETH  daily sell level: $1929 daily buy point: $1898\n$BNB  daily sell level: $610 daily buy point: $598\n$BTC #BTC $ETH #ETH",
